"glibc does not provide a wrapper for B<getdents>(); call B<getdents>()  "
"using B<syscall>(2).  In that case you will need to define the "
"I<linux_dirent> structure yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/getdents.2:244
msgid ""
"The B<getdents64>()  system call accepts an B<unsigned int> argument "
"I<count> and assumes that I<count> does not exceed B<INT_MAX>.  The glibc "
"wrapper function sets I<count> to B<INT_MAX> if it exceeds B<INT_MAX>.  "
"glibc defines a I<dirent64> structure, which is similar to I<linux_dirent64> "
"but with a 256-byte I<d_name>."
msgstr ""

